2026-05-05T14:19Z claude closed — done
--- body ---
`erg init` embeds only managed assets (README, spec, integration files, skills)
plus the pre-built bootstrap binary `tickets/tools/go/erg`. It never copies
Go source files (`*.go`, `go.mod`, `go.sum`) into target projects.

However, `erg check` has no guard against source files appearing there — e.g.
from a manual `cp -r` that included source, or a stale install attempt. A
project accumulating Go source in `tickets/tools/go/` is confusing and
unnecessary; only the binary matters at runtime.

**Desired behaviour:**
- `erg check` warns (non-fatal, printed to stdout) when it finds any `*.go`,
  `go.mod`, or `go.sum` files under `tickets/tools/go/`.
- Warning text: `WARN: Go source files found in tickets/tools/go/ — only the
  binary is needed; remove *.go, go.mod, go.sum`
- `erg check` does NOT remove them — auto-cleanup is out of scope.
- Exit code remains 0 (warning only, not a corpus error).

**Exception — git-erg project itself:**
If the project is the git-erg source repo, Go source files are expected and
the warning must be suppressed. Detection heuristic: read `tickets/tools/go/go.mod`
and check for `module github.com/MinhHaDuong/git-erg`. If that module path is
present, suppress the warning entirely.

**Implementation notes:**
- Add the check to `cmdCheck` in `check.go` (or wherever `erg check` lives).
- Use `os.ReadDir("tickets/tools/go")` and filter for Go file extensions.
- Read `go.mod` with `os.ReadFile`; `strings.Contains(content, "module github.com/MinhHaDuong/git-erg")` is sufficient.
- No new dependencies; no network calls.

**Tests:**
- Shell integration test in `tests/test_check.sh`: create a temp project dir
  with `tickets/tools/go/fake.go` present → verify warning appears in stdout.
- Same fixture but with a `go.mod` containing the git-erg module path → verify
  no warning.
